{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ואת בלעם בן בעור הקוסם", :translit "v'et bil'am ben b'or ha-kosem", :gloss "and Balaam son of Beor the sorcerer"} {:he "מכשפה לא תחיה", :translit "m'chashefah lo t'chiyeh", :gloss "a sorceress you shall not let live"} {:he "יש דרך ישר לפני איש ואחריתה דרכי מות", :translit "yesh derekh yashar lifnei ish v'acharitah darchei mavet", :gloss "there is a way straight before a man but its end ways of death"} {:he "יש דרך ישר", :translit "yesh derekh yashar", :gloss "there is a way straight"} {:he "שכר", :translit "s'char", :gloss "reward / wage"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :rashei-tevot, :phrase "יש דרך ישר", :spells "עולה כד"} {:kind :sofei-tevot, :phrase "יש דרך ישר", :spells "שכר"} {:kind :other, :note "Balaam's counsel caused 24,000 Israelite deaths per Numbers 25:9"}], :frame {:text "The phrase מכשפה לא תחיה appears in Exodus 22:17 as the prohibition against sorcery. Ba'al HaTurim applies it to Balaam, who is identified as a practitioner of sorcery (הקוסם) in this verse (Numbers 31:13). The verse from Proverbs 14:12 describes a path that appears straight but leads to death — the 24,000 Israelites who died in the plague at Shittim are recorded in Numbers 25:9. Ba'al HaTurim reads the acrostic and sof-tevot of that Proverbs phrase as encoding both the number 24 (thousand) and the word שכר, linking Balaam's 'straight' way to the wage he earned through counsel that caused Israel's loss.", :sources ["Exodus 22:17" "Numbers 25:9" "Numbers 31:13" "Proverbs 14:12"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :rashei-tevot, :phrase "יש דרך ישר", :spells "עולה כד", :letters ["י" "ד" "י"], :by :selah, :order :mismatch} {:kind :sofei-tevot, :phrase "יש דרך ישר", :spells "שכר", :letters ["ש" "ך" "ר"], :by :selah, :order :in-order} {:kind :other, :note "Balaam's counsel caused 24,000 Israelite deaths per Numbers 25:9", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2